From aa2d5ee627973e28d21dbb7cd1a4343488411f25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jino Abraham <jinoabraham26@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 13:53:57 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] spdm: Update device secret lib stub for libspdm 4.0

libspdm removed LIBSPDM_HAL_PASS_SPDM_CONTEXT, so every HAL callback now
takes the SPDM context as an unconditional first argument. Several
prototypes also gained post-quantum algorithm and key pair ID
parameters, libspdm_write_certificate_to_nvm was replaced by
libspdm_update_local_cert_chain, and libspdm_gen_csr_ex was folded into
libspdm_gen_csr. Update the stub to match.

Also implement the HAL hooks that were missing entirely: the responder
key exchange callbacks from keyexlib.h (a header the stub never
included), the PSK response opaque data callbacks,
libspdm_challenge_start_mut_auth and
libspdm_get_cert_chain_slot_storage_size. libspdm is built as a shared
library with no device secret library linked in, so it leaves these
undefined for the application to provide and spdmd failed to link
without them.

The stub now exports the same symbol set as libspdm's own
spdm_device_secret_lib_null, and keeps its return values: false, or 0
for the two non-boolean hooks.

Change-Id: Id01f85b2b12c9a11154a4a0aa8cca08f32538eda
Signed-off-by: Jino Abraham <jinoabraham26@gmail.com>
